# Pull requests

## Title

Conventional Commits: `type(optional-scope): subject`, in English (`.cursor/rules/conventional-commits.mdc`).

## Body

Follow `.github/pull_request_template.md` with the same headings in the same order:

1. `## Summary`
2. `## Related`
3. `## Verification`
4. `## SQL`
5. `## Risk / Rollback`
6. `## Checklist`

- The headings stay English. The body text may be Japanese (`.cursor/rules/language.mdc`).
- Empty sections say `N/A`; do not delete them.
- `## Related` has `Closes #N` alone on a line when the PR finishes the Issue, `Part of #N` when it does not (`.cursor/rules/github-closing.mdc`).
- A count in a PR body or comment (tests, mutants, cases) is counted from the output of that turn, not added up from memory.
- A commit SHA in a PR body or comment is copied from the `git` or `gh` output of that turn (`gh pr view <n> --json headRefOid`), never written from memory or guessed. A reply to a review once named a head that did not exist.
- A box under `## Verification` is checked for the head that it names, after that head's result is in: "CI green on every job" waits for the CI run of the pushed head to finish (`gh pr checks <n>`), not for the previous head's run. Right after a push, `gh pr checks` lists nothing and `--watch` returns at once: wait until the new head's runs are listed, then wait for them. On #79 the box was checked before the runs had started.
- `## Verification` names the commands that ran and their result: `./build.ps1`, the CI run (the merge gate), the NativeAOT publish when the Issue names it, any search an "every X does Y" claim rests on (`.cursor/rules/spec-checks.mdc`). A speed or memory claim carries its numbers here, before and after, against a named baseline (`.cursor/rules/open-ends.mdc`).
- `## SQL` lists each builder call whose generated SQL the PR adds or changes, with the SQL it renders per dialect, and for a change the SQL before and after. `N/A` only when no generated SQL changed.
- Pass the body to `gh pr create` through a temporary UTF-8 file (`--body-file`), deleted after the call (`.cursor/rules/scratch.mdc`).
